{"base_rate":0.6301188903566711,"brier":0.12085733157199473,"bss":0.4814527328541479,"bss_hi":0.5695023046850263,"bss_lo":0.3756924714440386,"country":"NO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09109643328929992,"ess":329.81043583169964,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Bergen</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Bergen rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>92%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBERGEN FLORIDA, 1.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.48, ranked 16 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(4&ndash;41) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>150</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>27%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>379</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Bergen</b> <span class=\"muted\">NO</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.48</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>4&ndash;41\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Bergen &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Bergen\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.0856,377.14666666666665 99.79038961038961,311.0909090909091 201.32216216216216,200.0 349.47532467532466,51.09090909090912 411.13134564643804,18.0 411.13134564643804,20.8812664907652 349.47532467532466,112.54545454545456 201.32216216216216,273.78378378378375 99.79038961038961,363.09090909090907 59.0856,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"152.63672391017172\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"152.63672391017172\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.0856,348.02666666666664 99.79038961038961,282.72727272727275 201.32216216216216,200.0 349.47532467532466,122.0 411.13134564643804,45.85224274406329\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 150 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.0856\" cy=\"348.02666666666664\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 27% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"99.79038961038961\" cy=\"282.72727272727275\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 40%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"201.32216216216216\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"349.47532467532466\" cy=\"122.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 92% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 379 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.13134564643804\" cy=\"45.85224274406329\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(63%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Bergen the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.61) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.31).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'>0.305</td><td class='num'>11.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>73%</td><td class='num'>0.438</td><td class='num'>7.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'>0.501</td><td class='num'>6.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'>0.610</td><td class='num'>6.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":60.39299,"lon":5.32415,"n":757,"n_cities":109,"name":"Bergen","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0030666666666666668,"n":150,"obs":0.09333333333333334,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2680000000000004,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.11805194805194805,"n":77,"obs":0.2727272727272727,"sig":true},{"hi":0.65,"lo":0.2680000000000004,"mean":0.4048648648648649,"n":74,"obs":0.5,"sig":false},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.65,"mean":0.8233766233766233,"n":77,"obs":0.7142857142857143,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9975461741424804,"n":379,"obs":0.9234828496042217,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.2,"rank":16,"rank_hi":41.0,"rank_lo":4.0,"reliability":0.008889651639436849,"resolution":0.1155507798427994,"slug":"bergen","station":"BERGEN FLORIDA","timezone":"Europe/Oslo"}